---
title: Societal Engagement
layout: base.njk
permalink: /en/societal-engagement/
lang: en
translationKey: societal_interaction
description: "Jari Laru's societal engagement brings together expert statements, open materials, media appearances, network work and decision-making around education, AI and learning."
pageStyles:
  - /css/societal-engagement-page.css
templateEngineOverride: njk
schemaType: CollectionPage
schemaAbout:
  - "@type": Thing
    name: Societal engagement
    description: Bringing research, teaching and expertise into public debate, preparation processes and educational practice.
  - "@type": Thing
    name: Educational development
    description: Research-based development work with teachers, schools and professional networks.
schemaMentions:
  - "@type": CollegeOrUniversity
    name: University of Oulu
    url: https://www.oulu.fi/
---

{% set statementItems = [] %}
{% for item in (collections.publications or []) %}
  {% if item.data.type == "lausunto" %}
    {% set _ = (statementItems.push(item), null) %}
  {% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% set featuredStatement = statementItems[0] %}
{% set expertMediaItems = (mediaArchive.expertAssignments or []) %}
{% set featuredExpertMedia = expertMediaItems[0] or (mediaArchive.guest or [])[0] %}
{% set featuredPresentation = (collections.presentations or [])[0] %}
{% set expertMediaCount = (mediaArchive.expertAssignments or []) | length %}
{% set publicConversationCount = ((mediaArchive.guest or []) | length) + ((mediaArchive.interviewer or []) | length) %}
{% set presentationCount = (collections.presentations or []) | length %}

<section class="engagement-hero">
  <div class="site-shell py-5">
    <div class="engagement-hero-layout">
      <div>
        <p class="engagement-eyebrow mb-2"><i class="bi bi-diagram-3-fill me-1"></i>The university's third mission</p>
        <h1 class="engagement-hero-title mb-3">Societal engagement turns research and teaching into shared work.</h1>
        <p class="engagement-hero-lead mb-3">University work does not stop at lectures or publications. I bring research-based knowledge and teaching expertise to teachers, schools, networks, preparation processes and public debate.</p>
        <p class="engagement-hero-text mb-4">This page shows routes into existing material. It is not a separate archive, but a way to see where expertise becomes conversations, statements, materials and decision-making work.</p>
        <div class="d-flex flex-wrap gap-2">
          <a class="btn btn-primary rounded-pill px-4" href="#routes">Three routes</a>
          <a class="btn btn-outline-secondary rounded-pill px-4" href="#evidence">See examples</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <aside class="engagement-hero-panel">
        <p class="engagement-panel-kicker">Engagement in practice</p>
        <dl class="engagement-kpi-grid mb-0">
          <div>
            <dd>{{ statementItems | length }}</dd>
            <dt>expert statements</dt>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dd>{{ expertMediaCount }}</dd>
            <dt>expert roles in media</dt>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dd>{{ presentationCount }}</dd>
            <dt>presentations and materials</dt>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dd>{{ publicConversationCount }}</dd>
            <dt>public conversation roles</dt>
          </div>
        </dl>
        <p class="engagement-panel-note mb-0">The figures show the breadth of the material. Impact comes from how these formats serve the same questions of education and learning.</p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<nav class="engagement-mobile-path" aria-label="Main sections on the societal engagement page">
  <a href="#routes">Routes</a>
  <a href="#evidence">Examples</a>
  <a href="#whole">Whole</a>
</nav>

<section class="engagement-section" id="routes">
  <div class="site-shell">
    <div class="engagement-section-head">
      <p class="engagement-eyebrow mb-1">Three routes</p>
      <h2>Expertise appears differently for different audiences</h2>
      <p class="mb-0">Choose the route based on whether you are looking for usable knowledge for educational practice, expert statements and public debate, or decision-making work. The underlying materials remain on their own stronger archive pages.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="engagement-route-grid">
      <article class="engagement-route-card engagement-route-card--materials">
        <span class="engagement-route-icon"><i class="bi bi-easel2-fill"></i></span>
        <p class="engagement-route-kicker">Educational development</p>
        <h3>Research knowledge in use with teachers, schools and networks</h3>
        <p>In training, talks and open materials, difficult topics such as AI literacy and digital pedagogy are translated into practices that fit everyday education.</p>
        <a href="/en/presentations/" class="engagement-route-link">Presentations and open materials <span aria-hidden="true">-></span></a>
      </article>
      <article class="engagement-route-card engagement-route-card--statements">
        <span class="engagement-route-icon"><i class="bi bi-chat-square-text-fill"></i></span>
        <p class="engagement-route-kicker">Public expertise</p>
        <h3>Research-based perspectives for preparation and public debate</h3>
        <p>Statements, writings, media appearances and expert assignments make questions of education, technology and AI visible outside the university as well.</p>
        <div class="engagement-route-actions">
          <a href="/en/writings/#lausunnot" class="engagement-route-link">Statements and commentary <span aria-hidden="true">-></span></a>
          <a href="/en/media/" class="engagement-route-link">Media <span aria-hidden="true">-></span></a>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="engagement-route-card engagement-route-card--politics">
        <span class="engagement-route-icon"><i class="bi bi-bank2"></i></span>
        <p class="engagement-route-kicker">Decision-making</p>
        <h3>Local public work is its own responsible role</h3>
        <p>In positions of trust, expertise meets practical decisions, services and long-term planning. Political material is openly available on its own page.</p>
        <a href="/en/politics/" class="engagement-route-link">Politics and decision-making <span aria-hidden="true">-></span></a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="engagement-section engagement-section--evidence" id="evidence">
  <div class="site-shell">
    <div class="engagement-section-head">
      <p class="engagement-eyebrow mb-1">From the material</p>
      <h2>Three examples of societal engagement in practice</h2>
      <p class="mb-0">These highlights come from the same collections as their main archives. They are not a definition of the whole work, but a quick route to current examples.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="engagement-evidence-grid">
      <article class="engagement-evidence-card">
        <p class="engagement-evidence-kicker"><i class="bi bi-file-earmark-text-fill me-1"></i>Preparation and commentary</p>
        <h3>Expert statements</h3>
        {% if featuredStatement %}
        <p class="engagement-evidence-meta">{{ featuredStatement.date | dateFormat }}</p>
        <h4><a href="{{ featuredStatement.data.url or featuredStatement.url }}">{{ featuredStatement.data.title }}</a></h4>
        <p>{{ featuredStatement.data.description or (featuredStatement.templateContent | excerpt) | truncate(230) }}</p>
        {% else %}
        <p>Statements bring research- and teaching-based perspectives into education policy preparation.</p>
        {% endif %}
        <a href="/en/writings/#lausunnot" class="engagement-card-link">All statements <span aria-hidden="true">-></span></a>
      </article>
      <article class="engagement-evidence-card">
        <p class="engagement-evidence-kicker"><i class="bi bi-mic-fill me-1"></i>Public debate</p>
        <h3>As an expert in media</h3>
        {% if featuredExpertMedia %}
        <p class="engagement-evidence-meta">{{ featuredExpertMedia.date | dateFormat }}{% if featuredExpertMedia.data.mediaOutlet %} · {{ featuredExpertMedia.data.mediaOutlet }}{% endif %}</p>
        <h4><a href="{{ featuredExpertMedia.data.sourceUrl or featuredExpertMedia.data.url or featuredExpertMedia.url }}">{{ featuredExpertMedia.data.title }}</a></h4>
        <p>{{ featuredExpertMedia.data.description or (featuredExpertMedia.content | excerpt) | truncate(230) }}</p>
        {% else %}
        <p>Media appearances and expert roles bring educational questions into public conversation.</p>
        {% endif %}
        <a href="/en/media/" class="engagement-card-link">All media appearances <span aria-hidden="true">-></span></a>
      </article>
      <article class="engagement-evidence-card">
        <p class="engagement-evidence-kicker"><i class="bi bi-people-fill me-1"></i>Educational development</p>
        <h3>Talks and open materials</h3>
        {% if featuredPresentation %}
        <p class="engagement-evidence-meta">{{ featuredPresentation.data.date | dateFormat }}{% if featuredPresentation.data.source %} · {{ featuredPresentation.data.source }}{% endif %}</p>
        <h4><a href="{{ featuredPresentation.data.url or featuredPresentation.url }}">{{ featuredPresentation.data.title }}</a></h4>
        <p>{{ featuredPresentation.data.description or (featuredPresentation.templateContent | excerpt) | truncate(230) }}</p>
        {% else %}
        <p>Presentations and materials make research-based perspectives usable in different educational contexts.</p>
        {% endif %}
        <a href="/en/presentations/" class="engagement-card-link">All presentations <span aria-hidden="true">-></span></a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="engagement-section" id="whole">
  <div class="site-shell">
    <div class="engagement-loop">
      <div class="engagement-loop-copy">
        <p class="engagement-eyebrow mb-1">Same work, different forms</p>
        <h2>Societal engagement is not decorative cream on top of research or teaching.</h2>
        <p>It is a way in which research questions become sharper through practical encounters, and teaching-based understanding returns to educational development. That is why materials, statements, media and decision-making meet on this page, even when their archives remain separate.</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="engagement-loop-steps">
        <li><span>Research</span><strong>Knowledge about learning, technology and education.</strong></li>
        <li><span>Teaching and development</span><strong>Bringing research into teaching, training and collaborative development.</strong></li>
        <li><span>Societal engagement</span><strong>Carrying perspectives into materials, conversations, preparation processes and decision-making.</strong></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="engagement-section engagement-section--sources">
  <div class="site-shell">
    <div class="engagement-sources">
      <div>
        <p class="engagement-eyebrow mb-1">Go deeper</p>
        <h2>When you need details, continue to the original collection.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="engagement-source-links">
        <a href="/en/presentations/">Presentations and materials</a>
        <a href="/en/writings/">Writings and statements</a>
        <a href="/en/media/">Media appearances</a>
        <a href="/en/politics/">Politics</a>
        <a href="/en/research/">Research</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
